    "termsOfUse": "This data can be accessed and reused by researchers affiliated with universities or no-profit, non-commercial organizations in the fields of linguistics, semiotics, sociology, anthropology, and affiliated fields.\nDue to their increased re-identification potential, the audio files in the corpus shall be facilitated to linguistic and relevant discipline-specific research where analyzing the audio content is pertinent. In these cases, the signing of a Data Sharing Agreement is necessary.   ",
    "restrictions": "Signing of a Data Sharing Agreement provided by the University of Groningen is part of the procedure for re-use of the audio files of the corpus. The agreement will enter into force as of the date both parties have signed it. The agreement will continue to be effective during the period that you possess the data. During that period, you cannot terminate the agreement. The University of Groningen may terminate the agreement if you have not cured a breach of the agreement within a reasonable period of being notified of such a breach. At the request of the University of Groningen, you will return or destroy all copies of the corpus' audio files. ",
    "termsOfAccess": "Audio files and transcripts of the interviews are under a restricted access procedure to protect the privacy of the corpus' participants. Requests can be done via this platform. You will be contacted by a DataverseNL data curator soon after your request. ",
    "fileAccessRequest": true,
